{
  // This file tracks discrepancies where the WIKI is incorrect and the API is correct.
  // These entries are excluded from comparison results to avoid re-reviewing validated data.
  //
  // Format: taskId -> array of field names that have been verified as correct in API
  // Each entry should include a comment with the verification source and date.
  //
  // Run `npx tsx scripts/wiki-compare.ts --all --cache` to check for stale entries.
  // Stale entries (wiki now matches API) will be flagged for removal.

  // Fuel Shortage - wiki claims a loyalty gate the client does not carry.
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Fuel_Shortage
  // 2026-09-10: the Requirements line reads "Must be Loyalty Level 1 to start this
  // quest" and names no trader, so it would be attributed to the quest giver by
  // inference. Both 1.1 captures serve the task with an empty `AvailableForStart` -
  // no `TraderLoyalty`, no `GlobalVariableValue`, no condition of any kind - and the
  // API serves `traderRequirements: []`. The "the gate hides in a global variable"
  // argument cannot apply where the client carries no start condition at all.
  '5a0327ba86f77456b9154236': ['traderRequirements'],

  // Chemical Experiments - same adjudication as Fuel Shortage.
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Chemical_Experiments
  // 2026-09-10: wiki reads "Obtain level 1 loyalty with Peacekeeper"; both 1.1
  // captures serve an empty `AvailableForStart` and the API serves
  // `traderRequirements: []`.
  '5a27bafb86f7741c73584017': ['traderRequirements'],

  // All This Filth... - wiki claims Jaeger LL4; nothing corroborates it.
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/All_This_Filth...
  // 2026-09-10: both 1.1 captures serve an empty `AvailableForStart`. Jaeger LL4 is
  // restrictive enough that shipping it unverified would hide a task players can
  // actually take, so the gate stays out until a capture shows it.
  '600302d73b897b11364cd161': ['traderRequirements'],

  // Insomnia - wiki claims a BEAR faction restriction the client contradicts.
  // Proof: https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Insomnia
  // 2026-09-10: the wiki added "This quest is only obtainable by [[BEAR]] PMCs."
  // on 2026-08-31 (revid 357247), but a USEC profile's quest list contains Insomnia
  // while containing 0 of the 6 BEAR-only tasks and all 6 USEC-only ones - so the
  // client is filtering by faction and is not filtering this quest. tarkov.dev
  // serves factionName "Any", matching the client. The same wiki edit calls
  // Counteraction "the USEC counterpart quest", which is really the USEC half of the
  // Our Own Land / Counteraction pair, the likely source of the confusion.
  '5c0bd01e86f7747cdd799e56': ['factionName'],
}
